# Aeron 1.54.2 publication-image loss metadata uses a sequence-lock protocol.
# on_gap_detected writes loss_term_id, loss_term_offset and loss_length between
# begin_loss_change and end_loss_change. send_pending_loss copies them and
# discards the copy if the generation changed. Those speculative plain accesses
# can overlap, so TSan reports them even with observable generation atomics.
# Match only the native access frame, never arbitrary callers of Aeron.
race_top:^aeron_publication_image_on_gap_detected$

# Gap scanning probes frame-length words at 32-byte intervals beyond an empty
# frame. A receiver can fill that hole with a longer packet while the scan reads
# words inside its payload. The scanner only uses those words to bound a gap;
# TSan reports its atomic probes against the receiver's payload memcpy.
# This header contains only the native gap scanner, including when inlined.
race_top:*/concurrent/aeron_term_gap_scanner.h$
